  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 4-Formylaminooxyvinylglycine may interact with HUVEC through a series of molecular targets. The drug is linked to the gastric inhibitory polypeptide, which in turn is targeted by another compound, 7-Methoxy-3-(4-Methoxyphenyl)Chromen-4-One, and finally by Bufobutanoic Acid. All these targets ultimately lead to HUVEC, indicating a potential pathway where 4-Formylaminooxyvinylglycine may exert its effects through these intermediaries. The mechanism appears to involve a cascade of molecular interactions, with HUVEC being a downstream target of multiple pathways. The evidence supports a role for 4-Formylaminooxyvinylglycine in modulating HUVEC activity through these targets, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
